louisville police have released a huge  batch of evidence from an investigation  of the raid  that killed briana taylor back in march  now it raises  brand new questions over why police  targeted her home  in an effort to prosecute her  ex-boyfriend a police lieutenant who  came to the scene after the shooting  told investigators quote  something really bad happened the  material includes more than 250 videos  and more than 4 000 pages of documents  our national correspondent jerica duncan  is following this story  yeah the documents graphic videos and  photographs were released wednesday as  the outcry for justice for briana taylor  continues this video shows a close-up  view of her boyfriend kenneth walker  outside taylor's home after she'd been  shot telling  officers his girlfriend is dead who has  any apartment  nobody my girlfriend is dead  moments later a swat team enters  taylor's apartment  they quickly determine it's a crime  scene we have to be mindful what we say  we're on camera now so  at the center of the case whether a  search warrant for taylor's home was  issued properly police records show the  warrants stemmed from taylor's  communication with ex-boyfriend  jamarcus glover who was the target of a  narcotics investigation  the release includes audiotape of a  jailhouse conversation on the day of the  raid between glover  and a woman identified as the mother of  his child  in it glover says he had not been in  touch with taylor  further calling into question the  justification for the raid  we ain't been no man we ain't been  around each other over two  months in the two months  and the interim police chief is  continuing her investigation into the  deadly raid  it could result in disciplinary actions  or even  firings meanwhile the fbi continues its  investigation  into possible civil rights violations  and an anonymous grand juror is waiting  to find out whether they can speak out  about the grand jury process  gail yeah there's still so many  unanswered questions in this case but i  want to look at that  tape again jerika that you just showed  us with kenneth walker you  when you hear that 9-1-1 call he's in  such anguish such pain he clearly  doesn't know what is happening that  night  so to see him that night with police  going you know my girlfriend's dead  he doesn't know what is happening yeah  he doesn't he really didn't and his  mother actually there's audio of her too  on the scene talking to officers about  what she said her son did which was call  her  and tell her how scared he was because  he didn't know what was going on  it's a heartbreaking story and still a  lot of people believe no justice in that  case at this time  thank you eureka
 

